I have located and examined the implementation you asked about.

**Current code**
`/Users/tijs/projects/local-model-bench/runner/runs/tmpmjq_ovuz/run/swift/Sources/NoteKit/NoteKit.swift`
```swift
public func extractTags(from text: String) -> [String] {
    return text.split(separator: " ")
        .filter { $0.hasPrefix("#") }
        .map { String($0.dropFirst()) }
}
```

**Why the two examples fail**

* `split(separator: " ")` only separates on the space character.
* `"shopping list,#urgent."` is split into `["shopping", "list,#urgent."]`. The second token does not start with `#`, so `#urgent` is missed. The trailing `.` would also be kept.
* `"(#ideas)"` is split into `["(#ideas)"]`. The token starts with `(` not `#`, so the tag is missed.

The existing tests in `/Users/tijs/projects/local-model-bench/runner/runs/tmpmjq_ovuz/run/swift/Tests/NoteKitTests/NoteKitTests.swift` only cover space-separated tags:
* `extractTags(from: "hello #world #swift") == ["world","swift"]`
* `extractTags(from: "just plain text") == []`

**What needs to change**
